                                    I prefer the leather one. The design is 
                                    <input type="text" id="g-c1-1" placeholder="(nice)" class="grammar-input mx-1 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-300 focus:border-violet-500 focus:outline-none w-28 text-center font-bold text-violet-700 text-sm bg-white">,
                                    and it looks 
                                    <input type="text" id="g-c1-2" placeholder="(expensive)" class="grammar-input mx-1 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-lg border-2 border-slate-300 focus:border-violet-500 focus:outline-none w-36 text-center font-bold text-violet-700 text-sm bg-white">
                                    than the wool one.
                                </div>
                            </div>
                            <div id="hint-c1" class="text-xs font-semibold hidden"></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Conversation 2 -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-5 sm:p-6 shadow-sm hover:border-violet-200 transition">
                    <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-4 border-b border-slate-100 mb-4">
                        <div class="flex items-center space-x-3">
